WEBVTT

00:00:00.895 --> 00:00:03.979
Chasing late invoices is the job nobody wants.

00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:08.068
Mugavi writes the reminders, but you approve every one first.

00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:11.554
Here is the whole flow in under a minute and a half.

00:00:12.505 --> 00:00:14.462
First, connect your books.

00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:19.730
Mugavi reads your customers and open invoices from QuickBooks or Xero.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.967
It never emails anyone just because it can.

00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:30.976
As soon as it syncs, your overdue invoices appear, oldest first, with what happens to each one next.

00:00:32.228 --> 00:00:37.836
The aged receivables report shows who owes what and how late, so you know where the money is stuck.

00:00:39.086 --> 00:00:46.043
On its daily run, Mugavi drafts the reminders that are due, in a tone that fits how late the invoice is.

00:00:46.043 --> 00:00:47.046
They wait here.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.989
Nothing goes to a customer until you say so.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.083
Read it, edit it if you like, then approve.

00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:58.712
After you press send, you get thirty seconds to undo before it leaves.

00:00:59.964 --> 00:01:07.522
When a customer replies, it lands in your inbox with a suggested next step, and reminders for that invoice pause until you have read it.

00:01:09.223 --> 00:01:13.965
That is Mugavi: reminders you approve first.

00:01:13.965 --> 00:01:14.396
com.

